{"id":"4efad838-b6a2-42c3-9c89-3d1d3758e1e3","object":"chat.completion","created":1785009467,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    mins = [s['minimum'] for s in segments]\\n    caps = [s['capacity'] for s in segments]\\n    sum_min = sum(mins)\\n    sum_cap = sum(caps)\\n    if budget < sum_min or budget > sum_cap:\\n        raise ValueError('Budget out of bounds')\\n    alloc = mins[:]\\n    remaining = budget - sum_min\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    importances = [s['importance'] for s in segments]\\n    capacities = caps\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        best_val = -1.0\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if alloc[i] >= capacities[i]:\\n                continue\\n            val = importances[i] / (alloc[i] + 1)\\n            if val > best_val:\\n                best_val = val\\n                best_idx = i\\n        if best_idx == -1:\\n            break\\n        alloc[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    by_name = {segments[i]['name']: alloc[i] for i in range(n)}\\n    total = sum(alloc)\\n    return {\\\"allocations\\\": alloc, \\\"by_name\\\": by_name, \\\"total\\\": total}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a Python function `solve(case)` that follows the specification. The case contains `segments` (list of objects with name, importance, minimum, capacity) and `budget`. We need to allocate budget to segments: first assign each segment its minimum quota. Then, while remaining budget > 0, allocate one token to the segment that maximizes importance divided by its next allocated position (i.e., number of tokens already allocated + 1? Or \"next allocated position\" meaning after adding one? Typically, such greedy allocation uses \"importance divided by (current allocation + 1)\" or something like that. The specification says: \"give one token to 